From: Dustin Kirkland <dustin.kirkland@chainguard.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] fix const-qualifier warning in translate()

strchr() with a const char* argument propagates const in newer GCC
built-ins, causing -Werror=discarded-qualifiers to fire on:

  utils/utils/string.c:33: char *match = strchr(from, *pos)

where `from` is const char*.  Fix by declaring `match` as const; the
pointer is only used for arithmetic (match - from), never to write
through it.

--- a/src/libstrongswan/utils/utils/string.c
+++ b/src/libstrongswan/utils/utils/string.c
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ char* translate(char *str, const char *from, const char *to)
 	while (pos && *pos)
 	{
-		char *match;
+		const char *match;
 		if ((match = strchr(from, *pos)) != NULL)
 		{
 			*pos = to[match - from];
 		}
